Just a quick note: I finally ascended a Slash'em character. Okay, it
was a doppelganger monk who found a wand of wishing, but she made it.

Since this was my first time anywhere near the end of Slash'em, I was
surprised.
Slash'em has the reputation for being very hard, but a lot of the
differences help you. Doppelgangers, techniques and mountains of loot
all make a difference. Gypsies pretty much guarantee you won't have to
ascend shorthanded.

Monks are good fighters. The "warning" numbers 1-5 were roughly the
number of times I had to hit them to kill them. And then there was the
crystal golem polymorph.

On the other hand, Demogorgon was a surprise. I polymorphed into a
basilisk. It didn't work at first. Demogorgon summoned some nasties,
and they killed the basilisk and peeled 400 HP off me before I got
back upstairs. This was a monk with a naked AC around -25.  Anyway,
that was the only tricky spot in the endgame.

Since I've ascended nearly all the interesting roles in Nethack, I'm
looking forward to playing some of the new ones in Slash'em.

--Milton


